    <string name="about_version">Version %1$s</string>
    <string name="about_developer">Developer: SenzaProject</string>
    <string name="about_package">Package: %1$s</string>
    <string name="about_description">A gaming assistant that shows real device readings and sets up each game your way.</string>
    <string name="about_limits_title">Known limitations</string>
    <string name="about_limits_body">The game library, per-game profiles, game modes, the floating panel with its dock, the toolbox, statistics, and device, network and FPS monitoring are in. Nothing has been tested on a real device yet. Game profiles change only brightness, Do Not Disturb, media volume and screen-awake, because Android does not let ordinary apps change CPU or GPU speed, so Game Master never claims to. FPS for a game needs a one-time ADB permission or root (root support arrives in phase 6). The latency number is a connection time, not in-game ping. Screen recording has no sound.</string>

