    <string name="fps_source_game">Game (advanced)</string>
    <string name="fps_display_explain">Counts the frames the display pipeline delivers to this screen each second. It shows the real display rate and any drops, but it does not measure a game. It keeps the screen redrawing while it runs, so stop it when you are done.</string>
    <string name="fps_game_explain">Reads SurfaceFlinger frame timestamps for the game you pick. Android only lets an app do this with the DUMP permission, which you grant once from a computer over ADB. This method is experimental and may not work on every phone or Android version.</string>
    <string name="fps_adb_title">One-time setup</string>
    <string name="fps_adb_body">Connect the phone to a computer with USB or wireless debugging turned on, then run this command:</string>
